Spec:
- Targets gain pre_build and post_build arrays of shell commands forming hook chain.
- Pre-hooks run before main command; post-hooks after successful main command.
- Hook failure stops chain and fails target immediately.
- All hooks and main command share target timeout as one deadline.
- Hooks can export variables by printing `BUILDCTL_ENV:KEY=VALUE` to stdout, KEY valid identifier. Malformed lines silently ignored. Exports carry forward to subsequent hooks in same chain. Pre-build exports also feed into main command's env and override same-named target env entries. Post-build hooks start from target's base env only -- pre-build exports do not carry over.

